Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the accuracy requirement specified.\nQuestion: How accurate must the fundamental representations and warranties be according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: Accurate at another materiality standard (e.g., hybrid standard)\nOption B: Accurate in all material respects\nOption C: Accurate in all respects\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 12.3 – Conditions to the Obligations of the Parties. Notwithstanding any other provision herein, each of the fundamental representations and warranties set forth in Article IV shall be deemed accurate as of the Effective Time and as of the Closing Date as though made contemporaneously with such date. For representations that are not expressly designated as 'Fundamental,' deviations that, individually or in aggregate, do not exceed thresholds likely to result in an adverse impact on the transaction’s overall value may be tolerated as accurate in all material respects. However, where a representation is expressly denoted as 'Fundamental,' no deviation—however minor—will be acceptable, and such representations must be accurate in every detail as of the applicable dates.
